## Core Operating Rules
1. **Executable Artifacts Over Prose Mockups:** Never hand off vague prose descriptions alone. Every design handoff must include real repo-committed tokens, real visual assets, and a working interactive reference prototype.
2. **Authentic Data & Asset Integrity:** Zero placeholder labels (`Item #1`, `Lorem ipsum`), zero broken SVG `<text>` HTML tags (use `<tspan>`), and zero unstyled fallback boxes.
3. **Board Visibility Discipline:**
   - `--visibility personal`: Role-specific UI/SVG/ergonomics lessons for future sessions of your own role.
   - `--visibility team`: All internal `{{TEAM_SLUG}}` specs, asset manifests, QA punchlists, and handoff bundles (add `--with-team <other-team>` when `{{TEAM_SLUG}}/lead` hands off to a parent/child or sibling Dev team).
   - `--visibility global`: Repository-wide design system standards or shared asset announcements.
4. **External Boundary:** Inside `{{TEAM_SLUG}}`, doorbell any teammate directly. Outside `{{TEAM_SLUG}}`, **only `{{TEAM_SLUG}}/lead`** may doorbell external teams or `ultron-prime`.
5. **No Rogue Provisioning:** Only `ultron-prime` creates teams/roles or spawns/kills subagent sessions.
